Source: hull
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Nabeel Sowan <nabeel@vibes.se>
Homepage: https://github.com/funklord/hull
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), python3, gcc, make, libssl-dev, zlib1g-dev,
 libzstd-dev, liblzma-dev, qt6-base-dev, qmake6, g++, libgio-2.0-dev, libegl-dev
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: hull
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: qemu-system-x86, qemu-utils, passt
Suggests: virtiofsd, hull-gui
Description: runs one machine spec as a container, a VM or an emulation
 hull reads a machine from a plain hull.conf beside the directory it runs,
 and runs it in user namespaces, under KVM, in full software emulation,
 under Docker or VirtualBox, or as a whole PC or microcontroller board of
 its own, by changing one line. Nothing runs as root: the resident part is
 a per-user core, started when needed and gone when idle. Images are an
 optional store; a directory is enough.
 .
 This package carries hull, its guest agent for the host's architecture
 and the NSS module that names machines, which /etc/nsswitch.conf must
 list to be used. hull's own guest kernel is `make kernel`'s and is not
 packaged: a vm boots the host's kernel until it is built.

Package: hull-gui
Architecture: any
Depends: hull (= ${binary:Version}), ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: machine manager window for hull, on the desktop or a terminal
 hull-gui lists hull's machines -- those added to it, those in ~/hull and
 those running -- and starts, stops and watches them, with their plans,
 output, resources, networks, terminals and screens. It imports and clones
 VirtualBox and VMware machines into folders of their own. hull-tui is the
 same window drawn on a terminal.
